Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:02:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sources: ciru re-derived 315 -> 15 and HELD with all 15
 reviewed (lane-156 GOAL 5)

currency's 315 is a with-merges range count over a fork that is both a sibling of
ROCmFPX and a mirror of upstream, so it triple-counts. Three subtractions:
274 (no merges) -> 129 (minus rocmfpx history, already covered by a CURRENT pin)
-> 15 (minus upstream/master). All 15 reviewed: 5 are upstream cherry-picks
ALREADY IN b10488 (each located by git log --grep), 4 are README/doc mass-dumps,
1 is a CI line, 1 is duplicate (lane-152 already took its SPIRV-Headers fallback).
The real queue for the next lane is THREE - c14872f84, 66afd2128, 0d313da18 -
with the DualView Q7 CUDA runtime held behind the President's park and this rig's
lack of CUDA. Held rather than re-pinned because the runbook allows a re-pin only
for SKIP.
---
 tools/arifi-sync/sources.json | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
index 6c2dfc7ad..84eea9593 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@
       "url": "https://github.com/ciru-ai/ROCmFPX",
       "ref": "ciru/main",
       "pin": "64d528be7",
+      "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane156": "PIN DELIBERATELY HELD at 64d528be7, and the number this row has been carrying is REFUTED. `currency` prints 'BEHIND by 315 commit(s)'. That is a range count WITH merges over a fork that is a SIBLING OF ROCmFPX AND A MIRROR OF UPSTREAM, so it triple-counts. Lane-156 re-derived it in three subtractions, each one command, all banked in research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-18-lane-156-currency2-proofs/goal5-ciru-real-delta.txt: `git rev-list --count --no-merges 64d528be7..ciru/main` = 274 (merges removed); `... --not rocmfpx/HEAD` = 129 (ciru-ai/ROCmFPX and charlie12345/ROCmFPX are the SAME PROJECT in two orgs, and that history is already covered by the reviewed `rocmfpx` pin, which is CURRENT); `... --not rocmfpx/HEAD upstream/master` = 15. FIFTEEN is the real unreviewed surface, not 315. ALL 15 ARE REVIEWED HERE. (a) FIVE ARE ALREADY IN OUR BASE - 01de1b421 (#26177), f15469a6f (#25832), 8a33d67b7 (#25830), 50265ff2a (#25643), 9307bd974 (#25611) are upstream cherry-picks, and each was found by `git log --grep` inside b10488: 0324696b8, dee2a846b, 2cfc7670e, c812c543f, 8bb909374. DUPLICATE, closed by this lane's bump itself. (b) FOUR ARE DOC/README MASS-DUMPS - b51512581, 09628016e, 36d659e1e (735/123 README plus ~4400 lines of docs/, a Dockerfile and CI), 112629f1e (179/682 README). NOISE. (c) 9b21a5512 is ONE CI line. NOISE. (d) 8ffb2cd5a's Vulkan half is DUPLICATE: its `find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG QUIET)` fallback plus GGML_VULKAN_SPIRV_HEADERS_INCLUDE_DIR is already in our ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt - lane-152 took it (series patch 0332) - CHECKED by string count (QUIET 1, the fallback var 3, the old CONFIG REQUIRED 0). Its remaining half is 24/5 in ggml-cuda.cu, off-rig. (e) c14872f84 'chat: trim messages sent to StepFun parser' - a common/chat.cpp parser fix with 50 lines of test; a real candidate, UNKNOWN against our chat.cpp and NOT closed here. (f) 9d91bc168 'Checkpoint tested DualView research runtime' - ~4500 lines, almost all ggml/src/ggml-cuda/** plus ggml/rocmfpx/**, the Q7 DualView panel/view runtime. It is CUDA (unbuildable on this Vulkan-only Beelink SER7 780M) AND the DualView/Ornith line is President-PARKED. NOT taken; the hardware half of that reason is the same standing constraint the 12 off-rig turboquant rows were ruled under. (g) 66afd2128 'Import selected ROCmFPX correctness and model fixes' and 0d313da18 'fix: preserve ROCmFPX features across upstream sync' ARE THE REAL REMAINDER AND THEY ARE NOT DECLINED. Between them: src/models/bailingmoe3.cpp +708, src/models/dflash.cpp +107/-6, laguna, llama-arch, an arg-parser surface with tests, tools/server/server-context.cpp +102/-4, and - the rig-relevant slice - ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp +24/-6, src/llama-context.cpp +162/-9, common/common.cpp +135/-13, common/speculative.cpp +67/-19. We HAVE all three model files at different (upstream) content, so every hunk needs per-hunk judgment against our tree; there is NO tip-state take here. That is a lane's work across ~18 files, not a rung, and the honest cost is why this pin is HELD rather than advanced: the runbook allows a re-pin only for SKIP, and (e) and (g) are UNKNOWN and blocked-TAKE respectively. WHAT THE NEXT LANE STARTS FROM: 15 commits, 10 of them already ruled DUPLICATE or NOISE above, so its real queue is THREE - c14872f84, 66afd2128, 0d313da18 - with 9d91bc168 held behind the President's DualView park and this rig's lack of CUDA.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_18_lane152": "PIN STILL NOT ADVANCED, but ONE of the two named keepers is now INGESTED: 8ffb2cd5a 'Fix Windows FP7 allocation and Vulkan configure' - the ggml-vulkan CMake half is ported (find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG QUIET) with a find_path fallback over Vulkan_INCLUDE_DIRS and $ENV{VULKAN_SDK}/Include, and a FATAL_ERROR that names the fix; link the imported target when present, include the found dir when not). Ours was still the hard REQUIRED at ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt line 14. FLAG C DOES NOT GATE THIS, checked rather than argued: FLAG C is a TYPE-ID dispute (ciru moved 107 to Q7_0_ROCMFPX against rocmfpx's Q2_0_ROCMFPX) and this diff touches no type id - it is CMake plus a ggml-cuda allocation change we did not take. The pin does NOT advance because the OTHER keeper, 0d313da18 'fix: preserve ROCmFPX features across upstream sync', is still READ-WORTHY-NOT-READ - it is the upstream-sync-preservation technique this file has flagged as 'exactly our problem' since the first note, it touches common/common.cpp and common/speculative.cpp, and this lane just spent its bump budget on the very problem it addresses. Advancing would assert a port-grade review that did not happen. FLAG C itself remains an OPEN HQ CALL and is untouched by this ingest.",
       "pin_review": "NEVER REVIEWED. Pinned to ciru/main as it stood on 2026-07-30, the day our own integration tree froze, so currency reports what has landed SINCE our port rather than this fork's entire re-imported history (pinning to its first commit reported 10,497, which is noise). The real figure: 273 commits in that window, of which 13 are ciru's own work and the rest are upstream they merged. Head 0d313da18 (2026-08-08) is 'fix: preserve ROCmFPX features across upstream sync' - exactly our problem; read it before the next upstream move. Also carries ActiveFPX PromptForge routes for Qwen3.8-27B. Shares NO ancestor with upstream llama.cpp: a re-import, not an ordinary fork.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "REVIEWED (r2, after checker BLOCK r1 findings F1/F2/F3). PIN STILL NOT ADVANCED - see the end of this key. TWO CORRECTIONS TO THIS LANE'S OWN r1 TEXT, both load-bearing. (F1) The claim 'ciru shares NO ancestor with upstream llama.cpp (a re-import, not a fork)' is FALSE AT HEAD. I inherited it from this file's older note and re-dated it without re-deriving - a stale-amendment. Re-derived now: merge-base ciru/main upstream/master = 15586e2d7 (Xuan-Son Nguyen, 'mtmd: add chunk save/load function (#26645)', 2026-08-06), and --is-ancestor returns 0 against both refs. rev-list --count ciru/main = 10499, of which only 201 are outside upstream/master - ciru shares ~10298 commits of upstream history. It IS an ordinary fork at HEAD, whatever it was when the older note was written. (F2) The '160 fork-authored' figure was WRONG BY ~10x: 145 of those 160 are ROCMFPX's OWN HISTORY, not ciru's. --not upstream/master subtracts upstream only, and this fork's own `role` field in this very file says 'ROCmFPX derivative' - the information needed to catch it was in the record being edited. CORRECTED FILTER, upstream AND sibling-fork history subtracted: `rev-list --count --no-merges 64d528be7..ciru/main --not upstream/master rocmfpx/main` = 15. CLASS SWEEP run across every row so the change is visibly ciru-only: prisml 2->2, rocmfpx 1->1, powerinfer 0->0, tq3 6->6, turboquant 151->151, tqplus 0->0, ciru 160->15 (delta 145). THE HONEST FIGURE IS A BRACKET, ~7 to ~15, not a new bare number: 15 subtracts upstream+rocmfpx and is itself a LOWER bound on ciru-authored work (it also removes anything ciru wrote that rocmfpx later merged); 7 is the strict %an=='Ciru' count. The bracket is tight because ciru's entire non-upstream history is only 201 commits. CONSEQUENCE: ciru is NOT the largest backlog and NOT one of 'two forks' - TURBOQUANT'S 151 IS THE LARGEST, and the fork-authored total is ~167-175, not 320. The r1 author histogram offered as a sanity check (caf 55, ciru-ai 54, charlie12345 13) ENDORSED THE ERROR - it was the histogram of the 145 contaminating commits, and charlie12345 is the rocmfpx repo OWNER. Fork-side is not the same as ciru-authored; that check is retired. GOAL-3 CIRU REVIEW, NOW PERFORMED against the real 15 (the r1 deferral rested on the inflated 160 and does not survive it). Ciru-authored (7): 0d313da18 'fix: preserve ROCmFPX features across upstream sync' (2026-08-08) - THE ONE TO READ, it is the upstream-sync-preservation technique this entry has flagged as 'exactly our problem' since the first note; touches common/common.cpp, common/speculative.cpp+h, and adds a check-rocmfpx.yml CI workflow. 8ffb2cd5a 'Fix Windows FP7 allocation and Vulkan configure' (2026-08-07) - OUR PLATFORM AND OUR BACKEND, a genuine build-robustness fix: makes find_package(SPIRV-Headers) QUIET instead of REQUIRED and falls back to searching Vulkan_INCLUDE_DIRS and $ENV{VULKAN_SDK}/Include, failing with a clear message instead of a hard configure error. Worth taking on its own merits. 36d659e1e 'Sync ROCmFPX with llama.cpp b10297' - the big sync, mostly docs/CI/Dockerfile, AND the commit that introduced FLAG C (see below). 66afd2128 'Import selected ROCmFPX correctness and model fixes' - an import FROM the sibling, so likely already covered by our rocmfpx pin. 9b21a5512 (CI one-liner), 09628016e + 112629f1e (README only, the latter -682 lines under the message 'submit') - noise. Non-Ciru (8): six are upstream PRs cherry-picked under new shas (#25611, #25643, #25830, #25832, #26177, StepFun trim) - the exact cherry-pick hole this lane documented, they are upstream work not ciru's; two are ciru-ai DualView research-runtime docs/checkpoint. NET: 2 commits worth reading, 1 sibling import, 4 noise, 8 not ciru's. NOT a lane of its own - the r1 open call saying so is WITHDRAWN. FLAG C, PROVENANCE NOW TRACED: ciru MOVED type id 107. rocmfpx/main, the ORIGINATOR, has Q2_0_ROCMFPX=107 and COUNT=108, matching TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 verbatim. ciru/main has Q7_0_ROCMFPX=107 and Q2_0_ROCMFPX=108, COUNT=109, and BOTH ids are in ciru's gguf-py GGMLQuantizationType - ciru WRITES GGUFs tagged 107 meaning Q7_0. Severity is LOUD, not silent: block_rocmfp7 static_asserts to 240 bytes per macroblock against block_rocmfp2 at QS_ROCMFP2+2 = 10 bytes / 32 values, so row sizes are nowhere near each other. The damage is to the RULE, not to a file: contract section 3.1 says serialized ids are 'not ours to choose - we adopt whatever the format's originator serialized', and ciru and rocmfpx are now two originators disagreeing about 107/108. HQ CALL OWED before ciru is ever used as a port source. FLAG C is CIRU'S OWN DECISION, not an inherited artifact: `log -S Q7_0_ROCMFPX ciru/main -- ggml/include/ggml.h` points at 36d659e1e (2026-08-06, authored by Ciru), one of the 7 ciru-authored commits above, and `branch -r --contains` shows it only on ciru refs. ciru renumbered 107 during its own b10297 sync. PIN NOT ADVANCED even though the 15 are now classified: 0d313da18 and 8ffb2cd5a are READ-WORTHY, not read - I named what they do from their diffs, and advancing the pin would assert a port-grade review of the sync-preservation technique that did not happen. The BEHIND row stays as the live signal, consistent with the prisml row in this same file. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
